{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790348157,"nonce":"gIW0NPuFxEtbfrnsb/JkFwpcvKQ=","title":"Bytecode output is not deterministic and plain .zbc does not record pointer width","message":"HashSet fields in HIR (hir.rs:298, :402, :1745) serialize in hash order, so the same module produces different bytes from run to run, which defeats content hashing and byte-level caching. Plain .zbc and ZPack files do not record the target pointer width; snapshots do (crates/zyntax_embed/src/snapshot.rs:173-183), so a .zbc built on a 64-bit host loads on a 32-bit one without complaint.\n\nUse ordered sets (or sort on serialize) for the serialized fields, and add the pointer width to the header or payload with a check on read.","files":null}]}